From 882efc5f93fd0e6df075a162cf0f4ef822a9cbfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:19:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: reverted-on-line disposition for protected-win
 registration (HQ87 Q89 (a))

An unregistered measured-win commit W in base..ref is exempt only when a later commit R in
base..ref names W by sha and is its exact inverse: replaying the reverse of every commit R names
onto R^ reproduces R's tree on every path they touch (registry JSONs and the generated series
excepted). validate prints it as REVERTED (W by R). A one-line difference, a reverse that does
not apply, or an R that does not name W leaves W UNREGISTERED (fail-closed). Tests: exact revert
GREEN, set revert on one file GREEN, one-line difference RED, unnamed inverse RED.

Deviation from the HQ87 wording (single-commit patch-id equality): b5dbcc886c reverts four commits
at once (78a3f7d19b + 7b1c2a88ca both edit ggml-vulkan.cpp), so no single reversed patch-id can
equal it; the replay over the named set is the same exactness test generalised to a set.

Origin: lane-298 (HQ87 2026-10-10 16:5x Q89 ruling)
Measured-effect: none - registration-gate tooling only, no engine code
---
 tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py      | 73 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/arifi-sync/test_arifi_sync.py | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 125 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

